    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0198" n="1032" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1032"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9493</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-20T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 21, 2.55 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4521. War Trade Board [from McFadden]:</p>
                <p>No. 284. The following is translation of a memorandum which the Italian delegate
                    on the Paris black-listing committee handed the committee at the meeting of July
                    19: <pb facs="0199" n="1033" xml:id="pg1033"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Italian Government declares that it has no objection to Japan’s
                            participating with the Allies in the formation of their black lists. It
                            believes that it is preferable, however, to have the information
                            concerning the Far East concentrated in Washington, following the
                            procedure adopted for America. The creation of black lists for China
                            should have the effect of doing away with the white lists.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>For your confidential information. The French enthusiastic about having a
                    Japanese delegate on the Paris committee. Please advise your views in connection
                    therewith. McFadden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
